WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.850
SCP-096, the Shy Guy, versus SCP-055, the
unknown object.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.599
SCP-055 is an anti-meme, meaning that it’s
impossible to remember any of its properties

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:11.730
after viewing it.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:16.920
When matched up against SCP-096, an anomalous
humanoid that attacks anything that sees its

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.840
face, it’s difficult to say who would come
out on top.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.750
If SCP-055 is alive, and placed in a room
with SCP-096, the Shy Guy would charge forward

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.050
with murderous intent, but as soon as it blinks
or looks away, the crazed creature would forget

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.119
about what it was running towards entirely.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:38.200
If SCP-055 is a mere object, SCP-096 would
have little interest in disposing of it, and

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:42.050
the two might be able to coexist in the same
containment chamber peacefully.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:46.680
Unfortunately, this is a matchup we may never
have a conclusive answer to.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.680
Wait…

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.210
What was SCP-096 fighting again?

